# oracle: fix shake on half the dimers and fix ilves on the other half: both switch their constrained bonds off (ebond 0; each fix's exclusions are kept), and velocity create after the fixes sees no fix ilves degrees of freedom before the first run (native builds the ilves constraint list at run setup), while fix shake's count from its definition
# oracle-inputs: w50il_dimer.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           real
atom_style      bond
read_data       w50il_dimer.data
pair_style      lj/cut 8.0
pair_coeff      * * 0.1 2.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 100.0 1.0
special_bonds   lj 0.0 1.0 1.0
neighbor        2.0 bin
timestep        1.0
group           ga id 1:64
group           gb id 65:128
fix             sh ga shake 1.0e-6 50 0 b 1
fix             cons gb ilves 1.0e-6 50 0 b 1
velocity        all create 300.0 4928 mom yes dist gaussian
fix             1 all nvt temp 300.0 300.0 100.0
thermo_style    custom step temp ke pe ebond press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             30
